Station H-01 (Survey Area H) consists of four interpreted resistivity layers. The sequence begins with a resistivity of 332.5 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$, which increases to 601.3 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$ in the second layer, before decreasing through the third layer (359.9 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$) and the fourth layer (286.0 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$).

Following the standard VES notation, the first three layers (1-2-3) follow a K-type pattern ($r_1 < r_2 > r_3$), and the subsequent three layers (2-3-4) follow a Q-type pattern ($r_2 > r_3 > r_4$). Consequently, the correct curve notation is KQ. The on-file classification of "K-type" is incomplete and does not accurately reflect the full resistivity profile of the station.

